VeridianOS: fix Solid compiler warnings (deprecated iterable, dead variable, null QPointer)

GCC reported, for the VeridianOS cross build (Qt 6.12):

- src/solid/devices/frontend/predicate.cpp:226, :227: 'QSequentialIterable'
  is deprecated: Use QMetaSequence's iterables and iterators instead
  [-Wdeprecated-declarations]. Ported to QMetaSequence::Iterable, which
  QVariant converts to through the same registered sequential-container
  converters and whose const iterator also yields QVariant elements.
  No behaviour change.
- src/solid/devices/backends/udisks2/udisksopticaldisc.cpp:41: variable
  'curr_record' set but not used [-Wunused-but-set-variable]. The counter is
  only incremented; remove it. No behaviour change.
- libstdc++ bits/atomic_base.h:658: '__atomic_sub_fetch_4' writing 4 bytes
  into a region of size 0 [-Wstringop-overflow], "destination object is
  likely at address zero", inlined from
  DeviceManagerPrivate::~DeviceManagerPrivate() (devicemanager.cpp:46).
  The destructor walks a copy of m_devicesMap, a hash of
  QPointer<DevicePrivate>, and called dev.data()->ref.deref() without
  checking the pointer, so a QPointer whose DevicePrivate is already gone
  would be dereferenced as nullptr. Every other lookup of m_devicesMap in
  this file checks the pointer first; the destructor now does the same.
  No change for live entries.

diff -ru a/src/solid/devices/backends/udisks2/udisksopticaldisc.cpp b/src/solid/devices/backends/udisks2/udisksopticaldisc.cpp
--- a/src/solid/devices/backends/udisks2/udisksopticaldisc.cpp	2026-10-08 17:12:14.455393617 -0400
+++ b/src/solid/devices/backends/udisks2/udisksopticaldisc.cpp	2026-10-08 17:12:14.537481661 -0400
@@ -37,8 +37,6 @@
     char dirname[256];
     /* our position into the path table */
     int pos = 0;
-    /* the path table record we're on */
-    int curr_record = 1;
     /* import debug category */
     using Solid::Backends::UDisks2::UDISKS2;
 
@@ -124,7 +122,6 @@
 
         /* update our position */
         pos += 8 + len_di;
-        curr_record++;
     }
 
     close(fd);
diff -ru a/src/solid/devices/frontend/devicemanager.cpp b/src/solid/devices/frontend/devicemanager.cpp
--- a/src/solid/devices/frontend/devicemanager.cpp	2026-10-08 17:12:14.488392317 -0400
+++ b/src/solid/devices/frontend/devicemanager.cpp	2026-10-08 17:13:36.338205120 -0400
@@ -43,7 +43,8 @@
     // take a copy as m_devicesMap is changed when DevicePrivate is destroyed
     const auto deviceMap = m_devicesMap;
     for (QPointer<DevicePrivate> dev : deviceMap) {
-        if (!dev.data()->ref.deref()) {
+        // A QPointer is null once its DevicePrivate is gone; skip it, as the other lookups here do.
+        if (dev && !dev->ref.deref()) {
             delete dev.data();
         }
     }
